{
	"_doc": "Spec 49 C0 fixture for §7.2 sizing (PS-2, PS-7, AC-3). Each case gives the settings at one device, the per-instance declarations the sizing atom's PHP and JS twins must print (PS-7 compares them as parsed declarations per property and device), and the box the browser draws in a 600px parent for a 1600x900 file unless the case names another file. 'root' is the `.{uid}` selector, used when the layout box and the surface are one element; a case with a wrapper gives 'layout' and 'surface' separately (the media element without a helper; the helper when printed); 'media' is `.{uid} .sgs-media-el`. Base rules in media-base.css are not per-instance and are listed once under 'base'. 'source' says where the expected box comes from: 'measured' (S-css-sizing.md and Q1-sizing-browsers.md, Chrome, Firefox and WebKit) or 'to-prove' (PS-2 decides; correct the case if it fails).",
	"context": {
		"parentWidth": 600,
		"file": {
			"width": 1600,
			"height": 900
		}
	},
	"base": {
		"media": {
			"height": "auto",
			"max-width": "100%",
			"min-width": "0",
			"box-sizing": "border-box"
		},
		"helperMedia": {
			"display": "block",
			"width": "100%",
			"height": "100%",
			"min-width": "0"
		}
	},
	"rules": [
		"Each set setting prints its own property.",
		"Default width per device from resolved values: nothing sizing-related set prints no width; Ratio and Height both set prints width:auto; anything else prints width:100%; a Width the user sets always wins.",
		"A helper printed with a Height, Width auto and no Ratio also prints the file's own ratio as aspect-ratio on the helper, per device.",
		"auto, natural or none at a narrower device cancels an inherited value by printing that keyword.",
		"A helper printed when nothing sizing-related resolves at a device also prints width:fit-content (PS-2).",
		"Cancel keywords: auto (Height, Width), natural (Ratio, printed aspect-ratio:auto), none (Max width and Max height print none; Min width and Min height print 0)."
	],
